Teach libpng's CMake build that DeBeOS/Haiku arm64 is arm64.

CMake derives CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR from `uname -p` on every platform
except Darwin and OpenBSD (Modules/CMakeDetermineSystem.cmake, the final
`else()` branch), falling back to `uname -m` only if `uname -p` *fails*.
Haiku's uname answers "other" for -p and exits 0, so the fallback never
runs and the architecture arrives in libpng's CMakeLists.txt as "other":

    -- Building for target architecture: other

That skips the whole `PNG_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE MATCHES "^(arm|aarch)"`
block, so arm/arm_init.c, arm/filter_neon_intrinsics.c and
arm/palette_neon_intrinsics.c are never compiled -- and, because the
same block is what would otherwise define PNG_ARM_NEON_OPT=0, pngpriv.h
goes on to enable the NEON code paths by itself from __ARM_NEON. The
result is a shared library with four undefined NEON symbols, which links
without complaint and then kills every consumer at load time:

    runtime_loader: /boot/home/lbdeps/lib/libpng16.so.16.53.0:
        Troubles relocating: Symbol not found
    $ nm -D -u libpng16.so.16.53.0 | grep neon
        U png_do_expand_palette_rgb8_neon
        U png_do_expand_palette_rgba8_neon
        U png_init_filter_functions_neon
        U png_riffle_palette_neon

`uname -m` does report arm64 here, so ask it directly rather than
disabling the optimizations: DeBeOS is ARM-first and the NEON filter and
palette-expansion paths are exactly the ones a browser's PNG decoding
spends its time in.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -122,6 +122,20 @@
 else()
   string(TOLOWER "${CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR}" PNG_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE)
 endif()
+# DeBeOS/Haiku: `uname -p` answers "other" and exits 0, so CMake never takes
+# its own `uname -m` fallback and CMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR is "other" on arm64.
+# Left alone that drops the ARM block below -- both the arm/*.c sources and
+# the PNG_ARM_NEON_OPT=0 that would have told pngpriv.h to stay off -- and the
+# library ends up referencing NEON symbols it never compiled.
+if(PNG_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE STREQUAL "other")
+  execute_process(COMMAND uname -m
+                  OUTPUT_VARIABLE PNG_HAIKU_UNAME_M
+                  OUTPUT_STRIP_TRAILING_WHITESPACE
+                  ERROR_QUIET)
+  if(PNG_HAIKU_UNAME_M)
+    string(TOLOWER "${PNG_HAIKU_UNAME_M}" PNG_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE)
+  endif()
+endif()
 message(STATUS "Building for target architecture: ${PNG_TARGET_ARCHITECTURE}")
 
